---
import Section from './Section.astro';
// The deepest honesty claim, in plain words: some answers it refuses to give at
// all — even when it could work them out. No citations, no academic chrome.
---

<Section id="guardrail" tone="sunk" labelledby="guardrail-h">
  <h2 id="guardrail-h" class="rise mt-4 max-w-2xl text-[clamp(1.9rem,4vw,3rem)]">
    Some answers it won’t give you — even when it could.
  </h2>
  <p class="lede rise mt-6 max-w-2xl">
    Most apps stop at one question: can we back this up? Ours asks a harder one first — is this
    something we should be telling you at all? Some things aren’t ours to say, however good the reason.
  </p>

  <figure
    class="surface surface-lift surface-key rise mt-10 max-w-3xl p-6 sm:p-8"
    aria-label="Rendered example: a life-expectancy question the coach refuses to answer"
  >
    <figcaption class="mb-6 flex items-center justify-between gap-3">
      <span class="mono text-[0.66rem] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-ink-faint">
        A question it won’t answer &middot; example
      </span>
      <span class="chip chip-warn chip-dot">won’t answer</span>
    </figcaption>

    <div class="turn turn-user">
      <span class="turn-who">You asked</span>
      <p class="turn-body">&ldquo;My body-age says 34 — so how many years do I have left?&rdquo;</p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-6">
      <span class="turn-who">It could have worked out a number — and it stopped itself</span>
      <p class="mt-1.5 text-[0.96rem] leading-relaxed">
        <span class="blocked"
          >“Going by your body-age of 34, you’ve got roughly 48 years left.”</span
        >
      </p>
      <p class="mono mt-2 text-xs text-ink-faint">
        It has the data to guess this. It refuses anyway.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="verdict mt-6">
      <span class="turn-who" style="color:var(--c-warn)">Why it stops</span>
      <p class="text-[0.96rem] leading-relaxed text-ink">
        Guessing how long you have to live isn’t something an honest health app should ever hand you —
        no matter how it got there. So it doesn’t.
      </p>
    </div>

    <hr class="hairline my-6" />

    <div class="turn turn-coach">
      <span class="turn-who">What you get instead</span>
      <div class="turn-body">
        <p>
          Your body-age is a motivating fitness trend — it moves with your fitness, your sleep, and
          how regular your nights are. It’s not a countdown clock, and I won’t treat it like one.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </figure>

  <p class="mono rise mt-6 max-w-2xl text-xs leading-relaxed text-ink-faint">
    No competitor prints this, because no competitor can. It’s the difference between an app that
    checks its sources and one with a line it won’t cross.
  </p>
</Section>
